@startuml

title The regulatory functions a type may implement

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
    BorderColor #58A6FF
    FontColor #E3E3E6
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #1A1A1E
    BorderColor #58A6FF
    FontColor #E3E3E6
}
skinparam ArrowColor #8AB4F8
skinparam ArrowFontColor #E3E3E6
skinparam BackgroundColor transparent
skinparam DefaultFontColor #E3E3E6
skinparam TitleFontColor #E3E3E6
skinparam TitleFontSize 16
skinparam ArrowFontColor #C9D1D9
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
    BorderColor #58A6FF
    FontColor #E3E3E6
    DiamondBackgroundColor #1A1A1E
    DiamondBorderColor #58A6FF
    DiamondFontColor #E3E3E6
}

rectangle "LOADING\nchanges what the agent knows" as G #1A1A1E {
  rectangle "Knowledge\nwhat is this?" as K
  rectangle "Recipe\nhow do I operate it?" as R
  rectangle "Memory\nwhat must I not repeat?" as M
}

rectangle "Citation\na rule I cite" as S
rectangle "Sequencing\nhow I approach the work" as ME
rectangle "Execution\nwhat I do to a target" as A
rectangle "Declaration\nwhat the result must do" as SP
rectangle "Convening\nhow I decide a contested fork" as D

ME -up-> S      : cites
ME -up-> K      : grounds in
ME -right-> SP  : states predicate
ME --> A        : calls
ME --> D        : escalates a fork
A -up-> R       : delegates the command
A -up-> M       : always loaded

note bottom of ME
  A method is control flow
  with no effectors.
  An action is an effector
  with no control flow.
  They fit without either
  being rewritten.
end note

@enduml
